---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import GdpChart from '../components/GdpChart.tsx';
import InflationChart from '../components/InflationChart.tsx';
import CentralBankDash from '../components/CentralBankDash.tsx';
import GlobalTradeViz from '../components/GlobalTradeViz.tsx';
import ScrollProgress from '../components/ScrollProgress.tsx';
---

<Layout title="Curriculum | GNEDHub">
    <!-- Snap Container -->
    <div class="h-screen w-full overflow-y-scroll snap-y snap-mandatory scroll-smooth relative no-scrollbar">
        
        <!-- Module 1 -->
        <section class="w-full min-h-screen snap-start flex items-center py-20 px-6 lg:px-12 relative">
            <div class="max-w-[1400px] w-full mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 lg:gap-24">
                <!-- Left: Content -->
                <div class="flex flex-col justify-center max-w-2xl">
                    <span class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-3 block">Module 1 &middot; 6 Min</span>
                    <h2 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 leading-tight">GDP & The Speed of Growth</h2>
                    
                    <div class="space-y-8">
                        <div class="bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/60 dark:border-white/5 shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.3)] p-6 rounded-2xl">
                            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Core Concept</h3>
                            <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-light">GDP measures the total dollar value of everything a country produces, acting as the ultimate scorecard for national economic health.</p>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-cyan-500 rounded-full"></span>
                                The Everyday Analogy
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-light">Think of GDP like a local bakery’s daily revenue. It counts the total value of all the bread, cakes, and coffee sold in a day. If revenue goes up, the bakery is thriving, the owner can hire more staff, and the town is happy. If revenue drops, the bakery has to cut back on flour orders and lay off the delivery driver. GDP is just this concept scaled up to an entire nation.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-cyan-500 rounded-full"></span>
                                The Scannable Lesson
                            </h3>
                            <ul class="space-y-5">
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">The Big Four Ingredients:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">GDP is calculated by adding up Consumer Spending, Business Investment, Government Spending, and Net Exports.</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Real vs. Nominal:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">"Nominal" counts raw numbers. "Real" GDP adjusts for inflation, telling the true story of growth.</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">The Recession Trigger:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">When real GDP shrinks for two consecutive quarters, the economy officially enters a recession.</span>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pt-6">
                            <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-medium italic"><span class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 not-italic uppercase text-xs tracking-widest block mb-1">Retention Check</span> If a country imports significantly more goods than it exports to the rest of the world, how does that imbalance directly impact its overall GDP "score"?</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
                <!-- Right: Interactive Sticky Zone -->
                <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 h-[500px] lg:h-[calc(100vh-12rem)] max-h-[800px] w-full bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/60 dark:border-white/5 shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.3)] rounded-3xl p-8 flex flex-col">
                    <div class="mb-6 flex justify-between items-center">
                        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wider">The Bakery Economy Slider</h4>
                        <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-cyan-50 dark:bg-cyan-900/30 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 text-xs font-semibold rounded-md border border-cyan-100 dark:border-cyan-800">Live Widget</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex-grow w-full relative">
                        <GdpChart client:load />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Module 2 -->
        <section class="w-full min-h-screen snap-start flex items-center py-20 px-6 lg:px-12 relative">
            <div class="max-w-[1400px] w-full mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 lg:gap-24">
                <div class="flex flex-col justify-center max-w-2xl">
                    <span class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-3 block">Module 2 &middot; 5 Min</span>
                    <h2 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 leading-tight">Inflation & The Invisible Tax</h2>
                    
                    <div class="space-y-8">
                        <div class="bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/60 dark:border-white/5 shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.3)] p-6 rounded-2xl">
                            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Core Concept</h3>
                            <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-light">Inflation is the gradual loss of purchasing power as the general price level of goods and services rises over time.</p>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-cyan-500 rounded-full"></span>
                                The Everyday Analogy
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-light">Imagine a cup of coffee stays the exact same physical size, but every year, the barista uses a slightly smaller measuring scoop for the beans. You hand over the exact same amount of money, but you get less caffeine. Inflation is the shrinking scoop; it means your money buys less today than it did yesterday.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-cyan-500 rounded-full"></span>
                                The Scannable Lesson
                            </h3>
                            <ul class="space-y-5">
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Demand-Pull Inflation:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">Too much money chasing too few goods. E.g., sudden bonuses spiking limited concert ticket prices.</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Cost-Push Inflation:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">Occurs when the cost to produce goods rises (e.g., a drought making wheat expensive).</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Wage-Price Spiral:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">A dangerous loop where rising living costs cause demands for higher wages, forcing further price hikes.</span>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pt-6">
                            <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-medium italic"><span class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 not-italic uppercase text-xs tracking-widest block mb-1">Retention Check</span> Why might central banks argue that a tiny bit of predictable inflation (around 2% a year) is healthier than zero inflation or deflation?</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 h-[500px] lg:h-[calc(100vh-12rem)] max-h-[800px] w-full bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/60 dark:border-white/5 shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.3)] rounded-3xl p-8 flex flex-col">
                    <div class="mb-6 flex justify-between items-center">
                        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Time-Travel Shopping Basket</h4>
                        <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-cyan-50 dark:bg-cyan-900/30 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 text-xs font-semibold rounded-md border border-cyan-100 dark:border-cyan-800">Live Widget</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex-grow w-full relative">
                        <InflationChart client:load />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Module 3 -->
        <section class="w-full min-h-screen snap-start flex items-center py-20 px-6 lg:px-12 relative">
            <div class="max-w-[1400px] w-full mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 lg:gap-24">
                <div class="flex flex-col justify-center max-w-2xl">
                    <span class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-3 block">Module 3 &middot; 7 Min</span>
                    <h2 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 leading-tight">Central Banks & The Cost of Money</h2>
                    
                    <div class="space-y-8">
                        <div class="bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/60 dark:border-white/5 shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.3)] p-6 rounded-2xl">
                            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Core Concept</h3>
                            <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-light">Monetary Policy is how central banks control the supply of money and adjust interest rates to either stimulate a sluggish economy or cool down an overheated one.</p>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-cyan-500 rounded-full"></span>
                                The Everyday Analogy
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-light">A Central Bank is like the driver of a car navigating a winding mountain road, using two pedals. The Gas Pedal (lowering interest rates) speeds up borrowing and spending. The Brake Pedal (raising interest rates) slows down borrowing to cool the engine.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-cyan-500 rounded-full"></span>
                                The Scannable Lesson
                            </h3>
                            <ul class="space-y-5">
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">The Base Rate:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">Central banks set the rate at which commercial banks lend to each other, dictating the cost of every mortgage and loan.</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Cheap Money:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">Low rates make borrowing cheap. People buy houses, boosting GDP but risking inflation.</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Expensive Money:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">High rates make borrowing painful. Spending stops, crushing inflation but risking a recession.</span>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pt-6">
                            <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-medium italic"><span class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 not-italic uppercase text-xs tracking-widest block mb-1">Retention Check</span> If the central bank hits the "brake pedal", who benefits immediately: someone saving cash, or someone trying to buy a house?</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 h-[500px] lg:h-[calc(100vh-12rem)] max-h-[800px] w-full bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/60 dark:border-white/5 shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.3)] rounded-3xl p-8 flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
                    <div class="w-full mb-6 flex justify-between items-center absolute top-8 left-8 right-8 px-0">
                        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Interest Rate Dashboard</h4>
                        <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-cyan-50 dark:bg-cyan-900/30 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 text-xs font-semibold rounded-md border border-cyan-100 dark:border-cyan-800">Live Widget</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="w-full">
                        <CentralBankDash client:load />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Module 4 -->
        <section class="w-full min-h-screen snap-start flex items-center py-20 px-6 lg:px-12 relative">
            <div class="max-w-[1400px] w-full mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 lg:gap-24">
                <div class="flex flex-col justify-center max-w-2xl">
                    <span class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-3 block">Module 4 &middot; 6 Min</span>
                    <h2 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 leading-tight">Global Trade & The Ripple Effect</h2>
                    
                    <div class="space-y-8">
                        <div class="bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/60 dark:border-white/5 shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.3)] p-6 rounded-2xl">
                            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Core Concept</h3>
                            <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-light">The modern global economy relies on highly interconnected Supply Chains where countries specialize in specific industries.</p>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-cyan-500 rounded-full"></span>
                                The Scannable Lesson
                            </h3>
                            <ul class="space-y-5">
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Comparative Advantage:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">Countries trade because it's mathematically efficient. Specialization increases overall global output.</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Supply Chain Shocks:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">A single blocked canal or regional crisis can shut down factories half a world away due to "Just-in-Time" delivery.</span>
                                </li>
                                <li class="relative pl-6">
                                    <div class="absolute w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-500 left-0 top-2"></div>
                                    <strong class="text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Tariffs & Protectionism:</strong> <span class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-light">Taxes on imported goods protect local jobs but inherently raise prices for everyday consumers.</span>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        
                        <div class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pt-6">
                            <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-medium italic"><span class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 not-italic uppercase text-xs tracking-widest block mb-1">Retention Check</span> If a government places a massive tariff on imported steel, who ultimately pays that tax?</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 h-[500px] lg:h-[calc(100vh-12rem)] max-h-[800px] w-full bg-white/70 dark:bg-slate-900/60 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/60 dark:border-white/5 shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.04)] dark:shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgb(0,0,0,0.3)] rounded-3xl p-8 flex flex-col justify-center">
                    <div class="w-full mb-6 flex justify-between items-center absolute top-8 left-8 right-8 px-0">
                        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Supply Chain Network</h4>
                        <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-cyan-50 dark:bg-cyan-900/30 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 text-xs font-semibold rounded-md border border-cyan-100 dark:border-cyan-800">Live Widget</span>
                    </div>
                    <GlobalTradeViz client:load />
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Minimal Floating Progress Pill -->
        <ScrollProgress client:load />
    </div>
</Layout>

<style>
    .no-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar {
        display: none;
    }
    .no-scrollbar {
        -ms-overflow-style: none;
        scrollbar-width: none;
    }
</style>